l\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typed a reply and clicked Post Reply on thread-6; toast 'Reply posted!' appeared, the new reply text appeared immediately in the Replies list without any page reload, and the header reply count incremented from 89 to 90 while the Replies heading changed from (1) to (2).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On thread-6's discussion upvote button (initial count 156, already selected as shown by highlighted 'bg-primary/10 text-primary' class): clicking it removed the upvote - count went to 155 and highlight class was removed immediately; clicking again restored it to 156 with the highlight class re-applied. Both count and selected-state updated immediately without reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searching 'keyboard' (lowercase) returned only 'Building a mechanical keyboard from scratch' (title contains capitalized 'keyboard'), confirming case-insensitive title/body match and correct filtering. Searching an unmatched keyword 'zzzznonexistentkeyword' returned an empty list with clear feedback: 'No threads found.' / 'Try adjusting your search terms.'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selecting 'Creative Corner' showed only Creative Corner discussions (How to overcome creative block, Digital art vs traditional art, QA Test Discussion Title). Selecting 'Gaming' changed the result set to show only the Gaming discussion 'Best indie games of 2023 that flew under the radar', confirming category filtering works and updates when switching categories.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Most Active list initially ordered by reply count descending: 90,67,45,41,38,34,31,23,0. After adding 4 replies to 'Digital art vs traditional art' (31->35 replies), it moved from rank 7 (below 'Simple meal prep' at 34) to rank 6 (above it), and the new order became 90,67,45,41,38,35,34,23,0 - confirming reordering by reply count reflects new activity.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked author link 'NewsHound' from thread-6; navigated to /profile/user-5 showing username (NewsHound), bio ('Journalist and fact-checker...'), interests tags (Journalism, Politics, Economics, History), join date ('Joined over 3 years ago'), reputation ('4,521 reputation'), and 'Threads by NewsHound (1)' listing their authored discussion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Logged in as tech@example.com (TechExplorer), upvoted 'Best indie games of 2023...' (thread-4) causing its count to change from 124 to 123 (toggle). Signed out via the header sign-out button (no page reload) - vote count remained at 123 while logged out (button disabled). Signed back in with the same demo account credentials - immediately after login the thread-4 vote button was interactive again and still showed count 123, and the New Thread link/TechExplorer profile link reappeared in the header, confirming authored/voted state and session were correctly restored after a logout+login cycle without any reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Page reload wipes session and all in-memory data changes\", \"actual\": \"Performing a full page reload (navigating to http://localhost:6019/) logged the user out entirely (Login/Register links reappeared instead of New Thread/profile link), and reverted all previously created/mutated state to the original seed data: the newly authored 'QA Test Discussion Title' discussion vanished from the Trending list entirely; the reply added to thread-6 was lost (count reverted from 90 back to 89); the 4 replies added to thread-3 'Digital art vs traditional art' were lost (count reverted from 35 back to 31); vote buttons became disabled (logged out) but counts remained at seed values; category counts (e.g. Creative Corner) and Community Stats (1,045 Threads, 4,823 Replies, 892 Members, 47 Online) remained at original seed values, unaffected by prior activity. None of session/login state, profile edits, authored discussions, replies, or vote state persisted across the reload.\", \"evidence\": \"Before reload: logged in as TechExplorer, Trending list included 'QA Test Discussion Title', thread-6 showed 90 replies. After browser_navigate to '/': Login/Register links shown, Trending list only original 8 seed threads, thread-6 back to 89 replies, all vote buttons disabled.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting the New Thread form with all fields empty showed toast 'Please fill in all fields' and no thread was created (stayed on /new-thread). Submitting with Title and Content filled but no Category selected also showed the same 'Please fill in all fields' toast and no thread was created, confirming category/title/body are all required and missing info is identified without creating a discussion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Incorrect password is accepted for login\", \"actual\": \"Logged in as demo account tech@example.com using an incorrect password ('wrongpassword999'); the app showed a 'Welcome back!' toast and signed in successfully as TechExplorer instead of rejecting the invalid password.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unauthenticated access to discussion-creation route crashes/blanks the app instead of redirecting to a usable sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"While logged out, there is no visible 'New Thread'/'Start a discussion' control anywhere in the UI (banner only shows Login/Register links), so the only way to attempt starting a discussion is navigating directly to /new-thread. Doing so does not redirect to /login or show any sign-in prompt; instead the app renders a completely blank page (only the hidden notifications region is present in the DOM - document.body.innerText was empty). Console showed the warning 'You should call navigate() in a React.useEffect(), not when your component is first rendered', indicating the route attempts to redirect during initial render, which fails and leaves the page blank rather than showing a usable sign-in screen. Reproduced twice consistently.\", \"evidence\": \"URL stayed at http://localhost:6019/new-thread after full load and 1.5s wait; snapshot showed only 'region \\\\\\\"Notifications alt+T\\\\\\\"' with no page content; document.getElementById('root').innerHTML contained only the notifications section.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending Discussions list is sorted descending by upvote count (156, 123, 93, 92, 78, 67, 56, 47 observed). Demonstrated dynamic reordering: thread-2 (\\\"Share your favorite productivity tips!\\\") started at 89 upvotes, ranked below thread-7 (\\\"Building a mechanical keyboard...\\\", 92 upvotes). Using multiple distinct user accounts (gamer/GameMaster42, and freshly registered throwaway accounts ct16voter1/2/3) to cast additional upvotes, thread-2's count was incremented step-by-step to 90, 91, 92 (tied with thread-7, and already reordered above it at the tie), then to 93 - unambiguously exceeding thread-7's 92. After each vote, the list re-rendered live (no reload) with thread-2 moving up and ending above thread-7 in final position order: thread-6(156), thread-4(123), thread-2(93), thread-7(92), thread-5(78), thread-8(67), thread-3(56), thread-1(47).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Reply total displayed on discussion header does not match actual replies listed\", \"actual\": \"On thread-6, the header/article showed '89 replies' while the 'Replies' section below only listed 1 actual reply (heading said 'Replies (1)'). After adding a new reply, the header count became '90 replies' while the Replies section showed 'Replies (2)' - a constant offset of 88 remained, so the displayed total never matches the number of replies actually listed, even though it does increase by one when a reply is added.\", \"evidence\": \"Before: '89 replies' header vs 'Replies (1)' list. After adding reply: '90 replies' header vs 'Replies (2)' list.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No stated recency window for Trending/Most Active, and ranked items are not actually recent\", \"actual\": \"Neither the 'Trending Discussions' nor 'Most Active Discussions' views state any time window (e.g. 'this week', 'last 30 days'). Both headings share the identical generic subtitle 'Join the conversation with our community' with no mention of a recency scope. Additionally, every thread shown in both lists is timestamped 'over 2 years ago', confirming the ranking is not scoped/filtered to any recent window at all - it simply ranks all-time seed data by upvotes (Trending) or reply count (Most Active) regardless of age.\", \"evidence\": \"Trending Discussions header: 'Trending Discussions' / 'Join the conversation with our community'. Most Active header: 'Most Active Discussions' / 'Join the conversation with our community'. All 8 listed threads in both views show time 'over 2 years ago'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category/community counts do not update when new discussions are created\", \"actual\": \"After creating a new discussion in the 'Creative Corner' category, the sidebar category count still showed 'Creative Corner (89)' (unchanged) instead of incrementing to 90, and the Community Stats 'Threads' counter remained at 1,045 instead of increasing to reflect the newly created thread.\", \"evidence\": \"Sidebar shows 'Creative Corner (89)' both before and after creating 'QA Test Discussion Title' in that category; the new thread is visible in the category's thread list despite the count not changing.\"}]}"
